    {
      "text": "Cr16Mn16Fe16Co16Ni16P20 tends to crystallize early during thermal analysis.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adding approximately 1–3 atomic percent boron will enhance the glass-forming ability of Cr16Mn16Fe16Co16Ni16P20.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Boron addition will increase the amorphous fraction retained after rapid cooling relative to the unmodified alloy.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Boron addition will delay crystallization onset during reheating relative to the unmodified alloy.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Boron produces enhanced short-range atomic packing.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Boron produces a denser and more disordered local atomic structure.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The boron-induced structural changes raise the energetic barrier to crystallite nucleation.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Boron disrupts short-range ordering by creating local atomic-size mismatches.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Boron facilitates stronger directional bonding in this alloy.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed size-mismatch and bonding effects increase the activation energy for crystallization during quenching.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed size-mismatch and bonding effects increase the activation energy for crystallization during reheating.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The beneficial effect is expected at cooling rates above approximately 10^3 K/s.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The beneficial effect is expected during reheating up to approximately 600°C.",
